3. Modify the boot sector: The boot sector contains a signature that identifies it as such. Your bootable program should be able to recognize this signature and copy itself to the boot sector, replacing the original one.


4. Add infection code: Your program should contain the code that will search for and infect other boot sectors on the system, possibly by copying itself to them.


5. Test your virus: Burn the bootable media (CD/DVD/USB) and test it on a computer to ensure it infects the boot sector and runs at startup.


